1
00:00:00,426 --> 00:00:03,426
(Howard:)how do you quantify
the strength of materials?

2
00:00:03,429 --> 00:00:05,059
(Sheldon:)Young's modulus.

3
00:00:05,064 --> 00:00:06,664
(Raj:)Is that right?

4
00:00:06,666 --> 00:00:08,796
(Sheldon:)Yeah.

5
00:00:10,270 --> 00:00:13,870
(Howard:)Okay, how do you prevent
eddy currents in a transformer?

6
00:00:13,873 --> 00:00:16,203
(Sheldon:)Laminate the core material.

7
00:00:16,209 --> 00:00:17,279
(Leonard:)Come on, give
him a hard one.

8
00:00:17,277 --> 00:00:18,977
That was a hard one.

9
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:21,950
(Sheldon:)All right.

10
00:00:21,948 --> 00:00:25,388
(Howard:)How does the flow rate in a pipe
depend on its diameter?

11
00:00:26,686 --> 00:00:29,586
(Howard:)You don't know, do you?

12
00:00:30,723 --> 00:00:31,793
(panting)

13
00:00:31,791 --> 00:00:33,161
(Howard:)What's the matter, smart guy?

14
00:00:33,159 --> 00:00:35,559
(Howard:)Don't know Poiseuille's law?

15
00:00:35,562 --> 00:00:37,632
(coughing)

16
00:00:41,234 --> 00:00:44,464
(gasps)
Thank goodness I got it!

17
00:00:47,140 --> 00:00:49,670
(Sheldon(coughing several times):)Now I can quit
checking my stool.

18
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:56,480
(Bernadette:)Okay, what are the
potential side effects

19
00:00:56,482 --> 00:00:58,512
(Bernadette:)for our erectile
dysfunction drug?

20
00:00:58,518 --> 00:01:00,988
(Penny:)Headaches, dizziness and nausea.

